PrometheusRule is a Kubernetes Custom Resource Definition (CRD) provided by the Prometheus Operator. It defines a set of alerting and recording rules for Prometheus within a Kubernetes environment.
The PrometheusRule resource allows you to manage and deploy alerting rules dynamically through Kubernetes, rather than editing Prometheus configurations manually.
Key Aspects of PrometheusRule
  API Version and Kind:
        The API version is monitoring.coreos.com/v1, and the kind is PrometheusRule.
        This indicates that it's a custom resource managed by the Prometheus Operator, which extends the Kubernetes API.
  Purpose:
        The PrometheusRule resource allows you to define:
            Alerting rules: Conditions under which Prometheus should generate alerts based on time-series data.
            Recording rules: Rules to precompute frequently used or complex PromQL queries and store the results as new time-series metrics.
        The advantage is that these rules can be managed directly within Kubernetes, using standard tools like kubectl, as part of the declarative configuration approach.
